                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "958b0d28-1c7b-42ef-8925-82f6ff256a7c",
                        "source_entry_id": "a640fab5-1421-30f9-8c74-4dfdf954b97f",
                        "source_sense_id": "608e2a69-9e17-3aae-9022-2ab56ec2d335",
                        "target_lang_word": "misogyny",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "misogyny",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a90a1bd9-d2da-3f1c-92eb-e5b36608bef5",
                                        "entry_id": "aef9f807-a57f-365a-89c0-ee88efae5c64",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Hatred of, contempt for, or prejudice against women."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e02de9af-0a1d-42fd-a90e-4790d3facfcc",
                                                "sense_id": "a90a1bd9-d2da-3f1c-92eb-e5b36608bef5",
                                                "text": "Although she argues against a simplistic conflation of types of prejudice, she suggests that misogyny is typically present in both narcissistic and obsessive forms of anti-Semitic prejudice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d23cba00-18b3-4c8f-b366-86f7eb0afa93",
                                                "sense_id": "a90a1bd9-d2da-3f1c-92eb-e5b36608bef5",
                                                "text": "His misogyny, like that of his predecessors, is more than prejudice; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4baf5e07-4524-4c3f-8354-18b0c1e0ef1a",
                                                "sense_id": "a90a1bd9-d2da-3f1c-92eb-e5b36608bef5",
                                                "text": "[…] a lonely straight male had no equivalently forgiving Theory of Masculinism to help him out of this bind, this key to all misogynies: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0ed0725-68fb-406b-bb0d-85c0548ea103",
                                                "sense_id": "a90a1bd9-d2da-3f1c-92eb-e5b36608bef5",
                                                "text": "This ontological symbiosis also explains his misogyny. By envying Sue, as the man he cannot become, he projects his self-loathing onto her, trying to diminish what he actually admires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f215bebb-d8df-4bf1-a2b8-20328eb1ee74",
                                                "sense_id": "a90a1bd9-d2da-3f1c-92eb-e5b36608bef5",
                                                "text": "[…] I have always found it hard that Hamlet, a character that I love and admire, is guilty of a puerile misogyny and, perhaps, more worryingly, of the unnecessary deaths of his old friends from university, Rosencrantz and Guildenstern. When I played him, I could find reasons for the misogyny but half-ignored the murders."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fabfdff2-b2ca-4526-86d4-b84ead7c98fa",
                        "source_entry_id": "a640fab5-1421-30f9-8c74-4dfdf954b97f",
                        "source_sense_id": "608e2a69-9e17-3aae-9022-2ab56ec2d335",
                        "target_lang_word": "misogynie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "misogynie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "62efeeda-90de-399b-ab84-9f1de347126d",
                                        "entry_id": "17e6a8b2-2557-325e-bea5-82a9bd616700",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Disposition hostile, méprisante ou haineuse envers les femmes, pouvant s’exprimer dans les discours, les comportements ou les structures sociales."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Études de genre"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9d6e543-99e7-452d-8690-c9a79276cd91",
                                                "sense_id": "62efeeda-90de-399b-ab84-9f1de347126d",
                                                "text": "De ce combat qui lui a fait mesurer la force de la misogynie, Mary Beard est ressortie avec la conviction que la parole des femmes dans l’espace public est une chose qui dérange."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "286f70a2-0253-4bce-b2ca-3d92343a51bf",
                                                "sense_id": "62efeeda-90de-399b-ab84-9f1de347126d",
                                                "text": "C’est en militant au sein de l’opposition que Nasrin Sotoudeh s’est rendu compte de la misogynie de la scène politique, même chez les dissidents. Dès le début des années 2000, l’avocate s’active au sein du mouvement féministe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b1866d8-5d34-43f7-b96a-f3d480601c2a",
                                                "sense_id": "62efeeda-90de-399b-ab84-9f1de347126d",
                                                "text": "C'est la fille d'un vicaire que nous envoyions affronter un homme d'affaires très dur, impitoyable, qui était là pour obtenir le meilleur accord pour les Américains… Il y avait plus qu'un relent de misogynie», se souvient l'un de ses conseillers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6607ac37-47d4-4f8c-aee8-0a3f33884768",
                        "source_entry_id": "a640fab5-1421-30f9-8c74-4dfdf954b97f",
                        "source_sense_id": "608e2a69-9e17-3aae-9022-2ab56ec2d335",
